/**
 * Cloudflare Workers Static Assets config for the Astro Starlight
 * documentation site at packages/docs-site-astro/.
 *
 * **Phase 6 status: deployed, accessed via service binding from
 * the legacy `annot-docs-site` worker.** Production
 * `annot.work/docs/*` still belongs to the legacy worker's
 * picker, but that picker forwards requests over to this
 * worker via a Cloudflare service binding when the
 * `annot-docs-stack=astro` cookie or `?docs-stack=astro`
 * query param opts in. After the 7-day observation window
 * (Phase 6.5 TODO in `docs/plans/annot-work-astro-unification.md`),
 * the picker is retired and this worker claims the route
 * directly; the VitePress sibling is then archived in Phase 7.
 *
 * URL layout after Phase 6:
 *
 *   annot.work/      → annot-marketing (landing)
 *   annot.work/app/* → annot (PWA at /app/)
 *   annot.work/docs/*→ annot-docs-site (legacy worker as picker)
 *                       ├─ default → its own VitePress assets
 *                       └─ opt-in  → THIS worker via service
 *                                    binding `ASTRO`
 *   annot.work/api/* → annot-api
 *
 * URL layout after Phase 6.5 (no more picker):
 *
 *   annot.work/docs/*→ THIS worker (Astro Starlight)
 *
 * Astro is configured with `base: "/docs/"` so every internal
 * link in the built HTML already includes that prefix.
 * `not_found_handling: "404-page"` because Astro emits a
 * per-route static file — falling through to an index page
 * would be wrong.
 */
{
  "name": "annot-docs-site-astro",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-04-23",
  "main": "./worker.js",
  // `workers_dev: true` keeps the
  // `<worker>.<account>.workers.dev` subdomain alive so the
  // operator can hit this worker directly during smoke tests
  // before the picker opts users in. The picker reaches this
  // worker via service binding regardless of `workers_dev`.
  "workers_dev": true,
  "preview_urls": true,
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  }
}
